Technical Troubleshooting Case: Veeam Backup Failure Due to vSphere Lifecycle Manager Snapshot Lock
Issue Summary
Error Message: "Unable to allocate processing resources. Error: No backup proxy is able to process this..."
Symptoms:

Veeam backup jobs failing on multiple VMs
Direct SAN connectivity confirmed working (ping successful)
Backups were functioning normally 40 minutes prior
No configuration changes made to environment
Issue did not affect all VMs uniformly

Root Cause Analysis
Discovery
Investigation revealed automatically created snapshots with the following description:
Snapshot generated by VMware vSphere Lifecycle Manager at 2026-01-04 21:13:43.666 
(Lifecycle Manager local time). Snapshot will not be automatically deleted.
The Trigger Event
At approximately 21:13 (9:13 PM), a batch VMware Tools update was initiated across multiple VMs simultaneously.
Update Results:

3 VMs: Reported successful update
1 VM: Reported failed update
Remaining VMs: No status event generated
Critical Finding: All VMs (including "successful" ones) were affected by backup failures

Technical Explanation
The Failure Chain

Snapshot Creation Phase

vSphere Lifecycle Manager (vLCM) initiated batch VMware Tools update
vLCM created protective snapshots on all target VMs before update operation
Snapshots flagged as "vLCM Managed" with exclusive maintenance lock


Update Execution Phase

VMs 1-3: Tools installation completed successfully
VM 4: Installation failed or hung
Remaining VMs: State ambiguous


Cleanup Failure (Root Cause)

Because the batch operation contained failures, the parent task never completed cleanly
vLCM failed to execute cleanup routine (Step 3 of atomic operation)
Snapshots remained in place with active maintenance locks
VMs flagged as "In Maintenance Transition" state persisted



Why Veeam Failed
vLCM snapshots create an exclusive lock on VM resources with special characteristics:

Lock Type: Maintenance transition flag
Effect: Prevents any external snapshot operations
API Response: vim.fault.TaskInProgress or vim.fault.InvalidState

Veeam's Failure Sequence:

Veeam backup proxy attempts to create snapshot for backup
Proxy queries vCenter for VM disk configuration access
vCenter responds: "Resource unavailable - host maintenance operation in progress"
Proxy reports to Veeam Manager: "Unable to allocate processing resources"
Backup job fails

Why This Occurs in Nested Labs
vSphere Lifecycle Manager has remediation settings designed for physical production environments that behave problematically in nested labs:

Feature: Quick Boot / VM snapshot during host maintenance
Physical Environment: VMs evacuated via vMotion before host remediation
Nested Lab Environment:

vMotion often unavailable or unreliable
vLCM falls back to snapshotting VMs for protection
Nested storage I/O insufficient for simultaneous snapshots of all VMs
Tasks timeout or hang, leaving snapshots orphaned with locks active



