Lessons Learned

Batch operations amplify failure impact - Single VM failure can affect entire group
Nested labs require special vLCM configuration - Default settings designed for physical infrastructure
Zombie tasks create persistent locks - Incomplete tasks don't self-heal
Snapshot orphaning is diagnostic indicator - Permanent "temporary" objects indicate crashed processes
Pre-backup snapshots should be external - Don't rely on vCenter-managed snapshots for protection during updates

